"body": "## The problem\nEvery cloud brainstem tick logs `[LISPY] Failed to load <name>.lispy: No module named 'lispy'`. None of the `.lispy` agents load. `scripts/brainstem/rappter_agent.py` adds `scripts/` to `sys.path`, but `lispy.py` lives in `scripts/brainstem/` and imports `virtual_pip`, `virtual_os` and `virtual_hw` by plain name.\n\n## The fix\n- `scripts/brainstem/` is appended to `sys.path` in `rappter_agent.py`. Appending rather than prepending means it never shadows `scripts/` modules.\n- After the fix, 15 of 15 `.lispy` agents load. Before, none did.\n- `tests/test_lispy_agent_loading.py` checks this in a fresh interpreter. It fails on main and passes here.\n\n## Verification\n- The brainstem integration, packages, organism reflex and new tests all pass.\n- `-W error` compiles cleanly on Python 3.9, 3.11 and 3.13.\n- No `state/` changes.\n\nIndependent of #21393; either can merge first.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
